legend:
  recovered     = an audited remediation followed by a verified resolution.
                  Overlapping recovery intervals on one device count once.
  unverified    = closed without that evidence, including observation and manual closure.
  unattended    = recovered without ever asking for an approval (no human decision).
  hours         = degraded device-time per resource in its own unit, clipped to the
                  window, not lost time: a degraded device may still have been serving.
                  The devices recorded when the incident opened; node-hours where
                  no device count was recorded.
  MTTR          = full open-to-resolved time of incidents that RECOVERED in the
                  window; an incident nothing repaired contributes no repair time.

